{#
/**
 * @file
 * Landing section: the markup for the paragraph types that draw it,
 * paragraph--landing-hero.html.twig (hero),
 * paragraph--landing-department.html.twig (department) and the older Bento
 * search (paragraph--bento-search.html.twig, the bento_search type, retired).
 * A search form that sends the search to the library's Bento results page
 * (its real name, kept below), and an optional Hill Memorial building map
 * under it.
 *
 * The form is a plain GET form: submitting opens landing_action
 * (https://lib.lsu.edu/bento) with the words in landing.identifier
 * (search_api_fulltext_bento), the same query Origami's search box sends.
 * There are no results on this page and no JavaScript; the result tiles
 * that palefire_modular builds (landing.tiles) are not printed.
 *
 * Variables from palefire_modular_preprocess_paragraph__bento_search():
 * - landing.identifier, landing.input_id, landing.placeholder
 * - bg_videos: ordered list of MP4 URLs (optional)
 * - bg_poster: poster image URL (optional)
 * - landing_map: the building_map paragraph from field_bento_map, rendered
 *   by palefire_preprocess_paragraph__bento_search() (optional).
 * - landing_intro, visit: the host Modular page's intro and Visit card
 *   (field_intro, field_hours_location, field_location_*), from
 *   _palefire_landing_visit() (optional).
 *
 * - page_title: the Modular page's title, set by
 *   palefire_preprocess_paragraph__bento_search() only when this landing is
 *   the page's first section. It is printed as the page <h1>, right above
 *   the intro; page.html.twig then prints no <h1> of its own.
 *
 * Layout, top to bottom, one 1280px column: the lead panel (title, intro,
 * search) on frosted glass, the building map, then the Visit strip (hours
 * from LibCal via visit-hours.js, mini map that loads on click with the
 * Google Maps link under it, an Instagram placeholder under the name), as
 * wide as the map's legend and drawing together. With a lead and
 * a map, .pf-landing--lead-screen: from md up the lead fills the first
 * screen and the page snaps between it and the map (landing-snap.js).
 *
 * - map_only: the paragraph's "Hide search panel" box (field_bento_hide_lead)
 *   is checked and there is a map. No lead panel: the map leads the landing.
 *   The page <h1> stays, visually hidden, so the page keeps its heading.
 *
 * - hero: set for the Landing hero paragraph (paragraph--landing-hero),
 *   .pf-landing--hero. The lead (.pf-landing__lead--hero) holds the title
 *   and today's hours, the intro, a "Search Special Collections" form (a
 *   placeholder: it searches Bento for now), the banners (the first the
 *   next event, from the events carousel's feed via hero-event.js, when
 *   there is one), then the Quick guide's A, B and C cards with
 *   the sign-in, then the map. No lead
 *   panel when it would be empty (no page title, no intro): the Next event
 *   card then stands alone.
 * - department: set for the Landing department paragraph
 *   (paragraph--landing-department), .pf-landing--department. The Bento
 *   search landing (search form, map, Visit strip), plus the hero's tile
 *   accordion under the search (includes/landing-exhibits.html.twig) when
 *   the paragraph has Tiles (hero_tiles).
 * - toc_home_id, toc_map_id: ids for the TOC's "Home" (the lead) and "Map"
 *   (the map) links, when this landing opens the page
 *   (PalefireHooks::heroTocIds()).
 *
 * "Search LSU Libraries" (not on the hero) and the map heading are h3s so
 * the TOC lists them.
 * While the map is in view, building-map.js adds .is-map-in-view here to
 * dim and blur the background video.
 */
#}
{#
  Index rule (.pf-index-rule, _landing-features.scss): a hairline with the
  section's number and name in the mono label voice, and at its right end
  an optional link (a running head, as in a catalogue). The numbers come
  from _palefire_hero_rules() in palefire.theme (hero_index here; the map's
  Rooms and access gets its own as map.visit.index), and the sections after
  the hero count on from them, so none is typed by hand. (Not a CSS
  counter: the map and the cover are size containers, which scope
  counters.) The number and name are decoration (the heading or list after
  each rule names the section), so only they are hidden from screen
  readers; the link is not.
  - link: { url, text, hidden (more of its name, read but not shown),
    external (opens in a new tab) }, or empty.
#}
{% macro index_rule(num, label, link) %}
  <div class="pf-index-rule">
    <span class="pf-index-rule__num" aria-hidden="true">{{ num }}</span>
    <span class="pf-index-rule__label" aria-hidden="true">{{ label }}</span>
    {%- if link.url %}
      <a class="pf-index-rule__link" href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>
        {{- link.text -}}
        {%- if link.hidden %}<span class="visually-hidden">{{ link.hidden }}</span>{% endif -%}
      </a>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}
{% import _self as pf %}
{% set landing_action = 'https://lib.lsu.edu/bento' %}
{% set landing_name = landing.identifier|default('search_api_fulltext_bento') %}
{% set input_id = landing.input_id|default('pf-landing-q') %}
{% set show_lead = not map_only and (not hero or page_title or landing_intro) %}
{# Next event (landing hero only), filled in by hero-event.js from the
   events carousel's feed; removed when the page has no carousel or no
   event. In the lead panel, or on its own glass when there is none. #}
{# Hero with its lead (cover): the video is a band at the top of the lead,
   behind the title, intro and search, washed into the page color like an exhibition
   cover, and the page scrolls on through the map in one flow (no glass
   panel, no snap). Other landings with a lead and a map: the lead fills
   the first screen and the page snaps between the two (md and up,
   _landing-swiss.scss, landing-snap.js). #}
{% set cover = hero and show_lead %}
{% set lead_screen = show_lead and landing_map and not cover %}
{% if lead_screen %}
  {{ attach_library('palefire/landing-snap') }}
{% endif %}
{% if hero %}
  {{ attach_library('palefire/hero-event') }}
  {% set hero_event %}
    <div class="pf-hero-event{{ not show_lead ? ' pf-hero-event--solo' }}" data-pf-hero-event>
      <p class="pf-hero-event__label">{{ 'Next event'|t }}</p>
    </div>
  {% endset %}
{% endif %}
<div{{ attributes.addClass('pf-landing', hero ? 'pf-landing--hero', cover ? 'pf-landing--cover', department ? 'pf-landing--department', bg_videos ? 'has-bg-video', not show_lead and landing_map ? 'pf-landing--map-only', lead_screen ? 'pf-landing--lead-screen') }} data-pf-landing>

  {% if bg_videos %}
    {{ attach_library('palefire/landing-video') }}
    {# The media layer: fixed behind the whole landing, or (cover) inside
       the lead's cover band, printed there below. #}
    {% set media %}
    <div class="pf-landing__media" data-landing-video data-sources="{{ bg_videos|json_encode }}">
      <video class="pf-landing__bg-video" muted playsinline preload="metadata"
             aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"
             {% if bg_poster %}poster="{{ bg_poster }}"{% endif %}></video>
    </div>
    {% endset %}
    {% if not cover %}{{ media }}{% endif %}
    {# Same look as the TOC hide/show button: icon square + a gold bar that
       fills as the current clip plays; the label slides out on
       hover/focus and is always read by screen readers. landing-video.js
       swaps the label and data-state.
       It sits beside .pf-landing__media, not inside it: the media layer is
       position: fixed with negative insets, so a button inside it was
       placed against the viewport and pushed off the right edge by the
       section padding (_landing.scss). With the breadcrumb in the lead
       (lead_breadcrumb) it moves into the sub-header bar instead. #}
    {% set video_toggle %}
    <button type="button" class="pf-landing__bg-toggle" data-landing-video-toggle data-state="playing">
      <span class="pf-landing__bg-toggle-progress" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <svg class="pf-landing__bg-toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <g class="pf-landing__bg-toggle-pause"><rect x="3.5" y="2.5" width="3.2" height="11" rx="1"/><rect x="9.3" y="2.5" width="3.2" height="11" rx="1"/></g>
        <path class="pf-landing__bg-toggle-play" d="M4.5 3.1v9.8c0 .8.9 1.3 1.6.9l7.6-4.9c.6-.4.6-1.3 0-1.7L6.1 2.2c-.7-.4-1.6.1-1.6.9z"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="pf-landing__bg-toggle-label" data-landing-video-label>{{ 'Pause background video'|t }}</span>
    </button>
    {% endset %}
    {% if not (show_lead and lead_breadcrumb) %}
      {{ video_toggle }}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if not show_lead %}
    {% if page_title %}
      <h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ page_title }}</h1>
    {% endif %}
    {{ hero_event }}
  {% else %}
  {# Title, intro and search on one frosted panel (the Visit card's glass),
     so the text reads over the background video. On the hero
     (_landing-features.scss), top to bottom: title, intro (full width), a
     search form, the two exhibitions, then Next event | Latest blog post.
     The lead's id is the TOC's "Home" target (toc_home_id,
     PalefireHooks::heroTocIds()). #}
  {% if hero %}
    {# PLACEHOLDER: there is no Special Collections search target yet, so
       the field and button are disabled (search_off) and the placeholder
       says so. When there is one, set landing_action / landing_name here,
       drop search_off and restore the placeholder ("Search manuscripts,
       rare books, photographs and more"). #}
    {% set search_label = 'Search Special Collections'|t %}
    {% set search_placeholder = 'Search coming soon'|t %}
    {% set search_off = true %}
  {% else %}
    {% set search_label = 'Search LSU Libraries'|t %}
    {% set search_placeholder = landing.placeholder|default('Search books, articles, databases, guides and more'|t) %}
    {% set search_off = false %}
  {% endif %}
  {# Sub-header bar: the breadcrumb on a glass bar across the content column
     right under the header (PalefireHooks::crumbInLanding(); page.html.twig
     leaves the head's breadcrumb out). Same markup and classes as the head's
     breadcrumb, so its type and link styles carry over
     (_landing-features.scss).
     The background video button follows in a sticky "dock": it starts at the
     far end of the bar's row and stays under the header while the landing
     (and its video) is on screen, like the TOC's hide/show button. After the
     breadcrumb in the source, so it comes after it in the tab order. #}
  {# Hero: the researcher card's "Log in" and "Register" (the Special
     Collections request system, Aeon; .pf-landing__account, below). Both
     open in a new tab (an up-right arrow; their names say so for screen
     readers). Aeon makes the account on a first log in, so Register goes
     to the same place until it has a page of its own (register_url).
     account_url: empty leaves the card out. #}
  {% set account_url = hero ? 'https://specialcollections.lib.lsu.edu/RemoteAuth/aeon.dll?' : '' %}
  {% set register_url = account_url %}
  {% if lead_breadcrumb %}
    <div class="pf-landing__bar">
      <div class="pf-landing__bar-inner">
        <div class="pf-breadcrumb pf-breadcrumb--modular pf-breadcrumb--lead">{{ lead_breadcrumb }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% if video_toggle %}
      <div class="pf-landing__dock">{{ video_toggle }}</div>
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  <div class="pf-landing__lead{{ hero ? ' pf-landing__lead--hero' }}"{% if toc_home_id %} id="{{ toc_home_id }}" tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>
    {# Hero: the title and the intro share .pf-landing__top: the intro
       under the title, beside it from xl (_landing-features.scss). Today's
       hours are a line under the title (below).
       The title is the TOC's "Landing" sub-link under Home, with the
       Quick Guide's heading the second (modular-toc.js). The headings
       themselves keep their own text and level. #}
    {# Cover: the video's layer, laid across the title, intro and search
       (_landing-features.scss, "Cover"). #}
    {% if cover %}{{ media }}{% endif %}
    {% if hero %}<div class="pf-landing__top">{% endif %}
    {# Hero: "LSU Libraries", a hairline, then the building (the Visit
       card's name) over the title as a small label, inside the <h1> so the
       heading reads "LSU Libraries, Hill Memorial Library: Special
       Collections" (_landing-swiss.scss, "Unit name"). The building is
       named here only, not again in the hours line. Theme colors only: no
       LSU purple or gold, which clash with the reading colors. #}
    {% if page_title %}
      <h1 class="pf-modular__title pf-landing__title"{% if hero %} data-toc data-toc-label="{{ 'Landing'|t }}"{% endif %}>
        {%- if hero -%}
          <span class="pf-landing__kicker">
            {{- 'LSU Libraries'|t -}}
            {%- if visit.name %}<span class="visually-hidden">, </span><span class="pf-landing__kicker-place">{{ visit.name }}</span>{% endif -%}
            <span class="visually-hidden">: </span>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- page_title -}}
      </h1>
    {% endif %}
    {# Hero: today's hours under the title: the status as a label (a dot in
       its color and the status in small capitals), then today's hours as a
       line of text (the building is in the label over the title; the
       script fills the status and
       the hours from LibCal; palefire/visit is attached with visit). No
       live region: the Visit panel already announces changes. Today's
       hours are the link to the week in the Visit panel (visit-strip.html.twig,
       the same {{ input_id }}-visit id in the map or under it); the hidden
       words finish its name, since the script fills only the hours. #}
    {% if hero and visit.lid %}
      <p class="pf-landing__hours" data-pf-hours data-lid="{{ visit.lid }}">
        <span class="pf-landing__hours-label">
          <span class="pf-landing__hours-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span data-pf-hours-status>{{ 'Hours'|t }}</span>
        </span>
        <a class="pf-landing__hours-link" href="#{{ input_id }}-visit-hours" data-pf-hours-jump><span class="pf-landing__hours-today" data-pf-hours-today></span><span class="visually-hidden">{{ ', this week’s hours'|t }}</span></a>
      </p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if landing_intro %}
      <div class="pf-landing__intro">
        {{- landing_intro -}}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {# Hero: the researcher card beside the intro, its foot on the intro's:
       a label, "Request items" (in the Reading Room or as digital copies),
       Log in and Register outlined (Log in with the stronger edge and
       an accent arrow; Search is the hero's one filled button), then a line to the
       guide for first-timers. On the five-column grid in columns 4-5
       (its end over the Search button's); narrower, the intro's other
       half; on phones, under it (_landing-features.scss). #}
    {% if account_url %}
      {% set account_id = input_id ~ '-account' %}
      {% set account_arrow %}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M7 17 17 7M8 7h9v9"/></svg>{% endset %}
      <section class="pf-landing__links pf-landing__account" aria-labelledby="{{ account_id }}">
        <p class="pf-landing__account-label">{{ 'Researcher account'|t }}</p>
        <h2 class="pf-landing__account-title" id="{{ account_id }}">{{ 'Request items'|t }}</h2>
        <ul class="pf-landing__account-actions" role="list">
          <li>
            <a class="pf-landing__account-button pf-landing__account-button--primary" href="{{ account_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              {{- 'Log in'|t -}}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ ' (opens in a new tab)'|t }}</span>
              {{- account_arrow -}}
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="pf-landing__account-button" href="{{ register_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              {{- 'Register'|t -}}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ ' (opens in a new tab)'|t }}</span>
              {{- account_arrow -}}
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="pf-landing__account-note">
          {{- 'First time?'|t }} <a href="{{ quick_guide.url|default('/v2/special/guides/special-collections') }}">{{ 'Read the guide'|t }}{% if not quick_guide.url %}<span class="visually-hidden">{{ ': How to Use Special Collections'|t }}</span>{% endif %}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    {% endif %}
    {% if hero %}</div>{% endif %}
    <form class="pf-landing__form" role="search" method="get" action="{{ landing_action }}" aria-labelledby="{{ input_id }}-heading">
      {# Hero: the label for screen readers only (the field and its placeholder
         say it on screen), so the links above sit close over the field. #}
      <h3 class="pf-landing__heading{{ hero ? ' visually-hidden' }}" id="{{ input_id }}-heading"{% if not hero %} data-toc{% endif %}>
        <label class="pf-landing__label" for="{{ input_id }}">{{ search_label }}</label>
      </h3>
      <div class="pf-landing__field">
        {# Hero: the magnifier is the button's icon instead, so none leads the
           field. Other landings keep it here and an arrow on the button. #}
        {% if not hero %}
          <svg class="pf-landing__field-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m15.5 15.5 5 5"/></svg>
        {% endif %}
        <input class="pf-landing__input" type="search" id="{{ input_id }}" name="{{ landing_name }}"
               placeholder="{{ search_placeholder }}"
               autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="search"{{ search_off ? ' disabled' }}>
        <button class="pf-landing__submit" type="submit"{{ search_off ? ' disabled' }}>
          <span class="pf-landing__submit-text">{{ 'Search'|t }}</span>
          {% if hero %}
            <svg class="pf-landing__submit-icon pf-landing__submit-icon--search" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m15.5 15.5 5 5"/></svg>
          {% else %}
            <svg class="pf-landing__submit-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
          {% endif %}
        </button>
      </div>
    </form>
    {# Landing department: the hero's tile accordion under the search, only
       when the paragraph has tiles (no placeholders). Its own wrapper, not
       .pf-landing__features, which turns the lead into the hero's
       full-screen panel. #}
    {% if department and hero_tiles %}
      <div class="pf-landing__tiles">
        {% include '@palefire/includes/landing-exhibits.html.twig' with { exhibitions: hero_tiles, label: 'Featured'|t } only %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if hero %}
      {# The exhibitions (once shown under the map as On view; kept for the
         landing department's tiles).
         - exhibitions: hero_tiles, the paragraph's Tiles (Hero tiles, each
           a Modular page or a Tile: _palefire_hero_tiles()), when it has
           any; else the PLACEHOLDERS below. Shape: label, title,
           start/end (ISO dates) and dates (shown), or permanent, or meta
           (a line in place of dates); more (the line shown when the tile
           opens); url and cta (the tile is a link only with a url); images
           (image render arrays; none: hatched frames stand in). More than
           one image crossfades (exhibit-rotate.js), with a pause button. #}
      {% set exhibitions = [
        {
          label: 'Exhibition'|t,
          title: 'Exhibition title'|t,
          start: '2026-09-01',
          end: '2026-12-19',
          dates: 'Sep 1 – Dec 19, 2026',
          more: 'Placeholder: a line or two about the exhibition.'|t,
          cta: 'View the exhibition'|t,
          url: '',
          images: [],
          frames: 1,
        },
        {
          label: 'Permanent exhibition'|t,
          title: 'LSU History'|t,
          permanent: true,
          more: 'Placeholder: a line or two about the permanent exhibition.'|t,
          cta: 'Visit the exhibition'|t,
          url: '',
          images: [],
          frames: 3,
        },
        {
          label: 'Guide'|t,
          title: 'How to use Special Collections'|t,
          meta: 'Registering · Requesting · Reading room'|t,
          more: 'Placeholder: what to bring, how to request materials before a visit, and the reading room rules.'|t,
          cta: 'Read the guide'|t,
          url: '',
          images: [],
          frames: 1,
        },
      ] %}
      {% if hero_tiles %}
        {% set exhibitions = hero_tiles %}
      {% endif %}

      {# Banners (.pf-hero-banners, _landing-features.scss): up to five tall
         banners under the search (four show on the 4-column grid, five on
         the 5-column one), straddling the cover's foot, offset unevenly,
         and rising in on load; narrower, a row to swipe. The picture is
         decoration: the words name the link.
         - First, the newest blog post (hero_blog,
           _palefire_hero_blog_banner()): its Image, else its date large.
         - Then the paragraph's optional Banners (hero_banners,
           _palefire_hero_banners()): Tile or Modular pages with their
           portrait cover, Category and title, linking as in a Tile
           showcase. The first of these holds the next event instead when
           there is one (js/hero-event.js, from the events feed); it is the
           backup. #}
      {% if hero_blog or hero_banners %}
        <ul class="pf-hero-banners" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'Highlights'|t }}">
          {% if hero_blog %}
            <li class="pf-hero-banner pf-hero-banner--blog">
              <a class="pf-hero-banner__link" href="{{ hero_blog.url }}">
                {% if hero_blog.image %}
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__media" aria-hidden="true">{{ hero_blog.image }}</span>
                {% else %}
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__media pf-hero-banner__media--date" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="pf-hero-banner__day">{{ hero_blog.day }}</span>
                    <span class="pf-hero-banner__month">{{ hero_blog.month }}</span>
                  </span>
                {% endif %}
                <span class="pf-hero-banner__text">
                  {# The label as the tiles' pill, no date on it; the date is
                     read here (any date set large is hidden from screen
                     readers). #}
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__label">
                    {{- 'From the blog'|t -}}
                    <span class="visually-hidden"> · <time datetime="{{ hero_blog.datetime }}">{{ hero_blog.date }}</time></span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__title">{{ hero_blog.title }}</span>
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {% endif %}
          {% for banner in hero_banners|slice(0, hero_blog ? 4 : 5) %}
            <li class="pf-hero-banner"{% if loop.first %} data-pf-hero-event{% endif %}>
              <a class="pf-hero-banner__link" href="{{ banner.url }}">
                {% if banner.image %}
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__media" aria-hidden="true">{{ banner.image }}</span>
                {% endif %}
                <span class="pf-hero-banner__text">
                  {% if banner.label %}
                    <span class="pf-hero-banner__label">{{ banner.label }}</span>
                  {% endif %}
                  <span class="pf-hero-banner__title">{{ banner.title }}</span>
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      {% endif %}


      {# Quick guide: under the banners, still in the lead panel. Index rule
         01 with the link to the full guide at its end, the heading and
         intro, then the three request paths, options A, B and C, from
         the full guide (the same include, so an edit there shows here too);
         on the hero's four columns, a timetable: heading and intro in the
         first, one option in each of the others. Close under the banners, so its heading
         shows in a laptop's first screen; the lead runs taller than the
         window, scrolls freely, and landing-snap.js snaps to the map once
         the lead's end is in view.
         - guide_url: the full "How to Use Special Collections" guide;
           empty leaves the link out.
         - quick_guide: title, intro, url and link_text from the paragraph's
           optional Quick Guide fields (_palefire_quick_guide()); each one
           left empty keeps the built-in text below. #}
      {% set guide_url = quick_guide.url|default('/v2/special/guides/special-collections') %}
      {% set quick_title = quick_guide.title|default('Quick Guide'|t) %}
      {% set quick_id = input_id ~ '-quick-guide' %}
      <div class="pf-quick-guide" aria-labelledby="{{ quick_id }}" role="region">
        {# Index rule 01, "Full guide" at its end. The full name keeps the
           visible words first (WCAG 2.5.3) and says which guide; with its
           own text or URL (the Link field) the link names itself. #}
        {{ pf.index_rule(hero_index.guide, 'Start your research'|t, guide_url ? {
          url: guide_url,
          text: quick_guide.link_text ?: 'Full guide'|t,
          hidden: quick_guide.link_text or quick_guide.url ? '' : ': How to Use Special Collections'|t,
        } : {}) }}
        {# The TOC label is the heading's own text once the title is set. #}
        <h2 class="pf-quick-guide__title" id="{{ quick_id }}" data-toc data-toc-label="{{ quick_guide.title ? quick_title : 'Quick guide'|t }}">{{ quick_title }}</h2>
        {% if quick_guide.intro %}
          <div class="pf-quick-guide__intro">{{ quick_guide.intro }}</div>
        {% else %}
          <p class="pf-quick-guide__intro">{{ 'Special Collections materials don’t circulate. Choose one of <strong>three ways</strong> to start: see it in the Reading Room (A), order a digital copy (B), or have a librarian help you find what you need first (C).'|t }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {# Before you visit: a few things first-time visitors ask, under the
           intro. The paragraph's optional field (quick_guide.visit) replaces
           the built-in list, each line of which the full guide states. #}
        <div class="pf-quick-guide__visit">
          <h3 class="pf-quick-guide__visit-title">{{ 'Before you visit'|t }}</h3>
          {% if quick_guide.visit %}
            {{ quick_guide.visit }}
          {% else %}
            <ul role="list">
              <li>{{ 'You don’t need to be affiliated with LSU: sign in or register as a Guest.'|t }}</li>
              <li>{{ 'Appointments aren’t required, but with one your materials are waiting when you arrive.'|t }}</li>
              <li>{{ 'Staff bring the materials to you in the Reading Room at Hill.'|t }}</li>
              <li>{{ 'Scans are 50 cents a page, plus a $10 fee per order, emailed in 5–7 business days.'|t }}</li>
            </ul>
          {% endif %}
          {# The full guide, the copy prices (palefire_guide_duplication.php)
             and the building's parking guide (visit.parking_url), as square
             buttons, each in a new tab: an up-right arrow after it, and its
             name says so for screen readers. #}
          {% set visit_links = [
            guide_url ? { url: guide_url, text: 'Full guide'|t },
            { url: '/v2/special/guides/duplication', text: 'Prices'|t },
            visit.parking_url ? { url: visit.parking_url, text: 'Parking'|t },
          ]|filter(link => link) %}
          <ul class="pf-quick-guide__links" role="list">
            {% for link in visit_links %}
              <li>
                <a class="pf-quick-guide__link" href="{{ link.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  {{- link.text -}}
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ ' (opens in a new tab)'|t }}</span>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M7 17 17 7M8 7h9v9"/></svg>
                </a>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
            {# Hours: "Hours" after a dot in today's status color
               (visit-hours.js), down to the week in the Visit panel, as the
               hero's hours line does (same page, so no new tab and the
               arrow points down). The status words are for screen readers
               only ("Open now, Hours"), so the dot's color never
               carries it alone (WCAG 1.4.1); the hero's badge shows them.
               The dot shows once LibCal answers; the button goes if LibCal
               fails, since the week does too. #}
            {% if hero and visit.lid %}
              <li class="pf-quick-guide__hours">
                <a class="pf-quick-guide__link pf-quick-guide__link--hours" href="#{{ input_id }}-visit-hours" data-pf-hours-jump data-pf-hours data-lid="{{ visit.lid }}">
                  <span class="pf-quick-guide__hours-status">
                    <span class="pf-quick-guide__hours-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden"><span data-pf-hours-status></span>, </span>
                  </span>
                  {{- 'Hours'|t -}}
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
                </a>
              </li>
            {% endif %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {# "Reach out" glides to the question form in the Ask Special
           Collections section further down (includes/ask-special.html.twig),
           which frames itself in gold, as the footer's Ask link does
           (js/footer.js). #}
        {% include '@palefire/includes/guide-request-paths.html.twig' with { uid: quick_id, img_base: file_url(directory) ~ '/images/guides/special-collections/', ask_href: '#ask-question' } only %}
        {# Phones: the paths fold to their first option under a fade, and
           this shows the rest (js/palefire.js; without it, all show). #}
        <button type="button" class="pf-quick-guide__expand" aria-expanded="true">{{ 'Show all steps'|t }}</button>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if landing_map %}
    <div class="pf-landing__visit"{% if toc_map_id %} id="{{ toc_map_id }}" tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>
      {%- if hero -%}
        {# Index rule 02: directions in Google Maps, as the Visit panel's
           link, in a new tab. #}
        {{ pf.index_rule(hero_index.visit, 'Visit Hill'|t, visit.maps_url ? {
          url: visit.maps_url,
          text: 'Directions'|t,
          hidden: ' ' ~ 'to @place (opens in a new tab)'|t({ '@place': visit.name }),
          external: true,
        } : {}) }}
      {%- endif -%}
      {{ landing_map }}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {# Visit strip: under the map, as wide as legend + map. On the hero the
     map shows it itself, under the drawing with its legend
     (visit_in_map, palefire_preprocess_paragraph__landing_hero()). #}
  {% if visit and not visit_in_map %}
    {% include '@palefire/includes/visit-strip.html.twig' with { visit: visit, visit_id: input_id ~ '-visit', keyed: false } only %}
  {% endif %}

  {# The hero's On view (exhibition tiles under the map) was removed
     (2026-10-22): the banners and From the stacks show the exhibitions. #}
</div>
